{{--
    Brand icon for one social platform — the portfolio theme's replacement for the
    two-letter text abbreviations ("FB", "IG", "TT") it used to print.

    Two-letter monograms are the single most recognisable tell of a template
    portfolio: nobody serious brands their LinkedIn link with the letters "IN".
    These are the real marks, inlined because an icon font or a sprite sheet is a
    network request and a flash of missing glyph for six glyphs.

    Falls back to the platform's first letter for anything not in the map, since
    the admin can add a platform this theme has never heard of (Social Links
    takes a free-text platform) — a plain initial in the same box is a far better
    failure than an empty one.

    Usage:
        @include('frontend.themes.portfolio.partials.social-icon', [
            'platform' => 'github',
            'class' => 'h-4 w-4',
        ])

    The marks are single-path, so they inherit `currentColor` and need no
    per-brand fill; that is also why every one of them is drawn on a 24x24 grid
    with a consistent optical weight.
--}}
